### name: link.binder.eszett-is-not-the-ss-binder
--- note
Review 2026-09-25 SQL-02. In memory _["ß"] is E_NO_KEY: no binder is named ß.
JS and Python upper-cased with Unicode rules (ß → SS) and translated it as the
SS binder. A qualifier is compared ASCII-case-insensitively, like every name.
--- dialect
sqlite
--- bindings
{"R": {"kind": "relation", "from": "r", "alias": "r", "fields": {"ID": {"column": "id", "type": "NUM"}, "VAL": {"column": "val", "type": "NUM"}}},
 "S": {"kind": "relation", "from": "s", "alias": "s", "fields": {"ID": {"column": "id", "type": "NUM"}, "VAL": {"column": "val", "type": "NUM"}}}}
--- as
statement
--- source
R .> LINK(S, SS, X, SS["ID"] == X["ID"]) .> MAP(RECORD("picked", _["ß"]["VAL"]))
--- error
E_SQL_SHAPE 1:67
===
