 "S": {"kind": "relation", "from": "s", "alias": "s", "fields": {"ID": {"column": "id", "type": "NUM"}, "VAL": {"column": "val", "type": "NUM"}}}}
--- as
statement
--- source
R .> LINK(S, SS, X, SS["ID"] == X["ID"]) .> MAP(RECORD("picked", _["ſS"]["VAL"]))
--- error
E_SQL_SHAPE 1:67
===

### name: link.binder.a-field-the-relation-lacks-is-refused
--- note
A qualified read of a field the named relation does not have is E_SQL_BINDING.
Lisp rendered it as a column the table lacks; the SQL fuzzer's link-binder
family found it.
--- dialect
sqlite
--- bindings
{"R": {"kind": "relation", "from": "r", "alias": "r", "fields": {"ID": {"column": "id", "type": "NUM"}, "VAL": {"column": "val", "type": "NUM"}}},
 "S": {"kind": "relation", "from": "s", "alias": "s", "fields": {"ID": {"column": "id", "type": "NUM"}, "VAL": {"column": "val", "type": "NUM"}}}}
--- as
statement
--- source
R .> LINK(S, SS, X, SS["ID"] == X["ID"]) .> MAP(RECORD("p", _["X"]["NOPE"]))
--- error
E_SQL_BINDING 1:67
===

### name: link.refusal.an-earlier-step-refuses-first
--- note
The sort reads a field SELECT_COLS dropped, and the LINK's key reads another:
the earlier step's refusal is the one reported. Lisp checked the sort's key only
when rendering, after the LINK's predicate.
--- dialect
sqlite
--- bindings
{"R": {"kind": "relation", "from": "r", "alias": "r", "fields": {"ID": {"column": "id", "type": "NUM"}, "VAL": {"column": "val", "type": "NUM"}}},
 "S": {"kind": "relation", "from": "s", "alias": "s", "fields": {"ID": {"column": "id", "type": "NUM"}, "VAL": {"column": "val", "type": "NUM"}}}}
--- as
statement
--- source
R .> SELECT_COLS("VAL") .> SORT_BY(_["ID"]) .> LINK(S, _1["ID"] == _2["ID"])
--- error
E_SQL_BINDING 1:37
===
